# ZyraVision Mobile — API Integration

## Overview
The mobile app communicates with the ZyraVision Laravel 11 backend via a REST API at `/api/v1/`. Authentication uses Laravel Sanctum with Bearer tokens. All API code lives in the Data layer (`lib/data/`).

## Base Configuration

### Environment
```dart
// Base URL loaded from environment at build time
// .env.development: API_BASE_URL=https://dev-api.zyravision.com
// .env.staging:     API_BASE_URL=https://staging-api.zyravision.com
// .env.production:  API_BASE_URL=https://api.zyravision.com

const apiBaseUrl = String.fromEnvironment('API_BASE_URL');
```

### Timeouts
| Timeout | Duration | Purpose |
|---------|----------|---------|
| Connect | 10 seconds | TCP connection establishment |
| Receive | 30 seconds | Standard API response |
| Send | 30 seconds | Upload requests |
| Stream | 120 seconds | Video stream / long-running downloads |

### Dio Instance
```dart
final dioProvider = Provider<Dio>((ref) {
  final dio = Dio(BaseOptions(
    baseUrl: '$apiBaseUrl/api/v1',
    connectTimeout: const Duration(seconds: 10),
    receiveTimeout: const Duration(seconds: 30),
    sendTimeout: const Duration(seconds: 30),
    headers: {
      'Accept': 'application/json',
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    },
  ));

  dio.interceptors.addAll([
    ref.read(authInterceptorProvider),
    ref.read(mobileHeadersInterceptorProvider),
    ref.read(retryInterceptorProvider),
    ref.read(etagCacheInterceptorProvider),
    ref.read(errorInterceptorProvider),
    if (kDebugMode) ref.read(loggingInterceptorProvider),
  ]);

  return dio;
});
```

## Interceptors

### 1. Auth Interceptor
- Adds `Authorization: Bearer {token}` to every request.
- Reads token from `flutter_secure_storage`.

```dart
class AuthInterceptor extends Interceptor {
  @override
  void onRequest(RequestOptions options, RequestInterceptorHandler handler) {
    final token = _tokenStore.accessToken;
    if (token != null) {
      options.headers['Authorization'] = 'Bearer $token';
    }
    handler.next(options);
  }
}
```

### 2. Token Refresh on 401
- On 401 response, attempt to refresh the token.
- Queue all pending requests while refresh is in progress.
- Retry queued requests with the new token.
- If refresh fails, clear auth state and redirect to login.

```dart
@override
void onError(DioException err, ErrorInterceptorHandler handler) async {
  if (err.response?.statusCode == 401 && !_isRefreshing) {
    _isRefreshing = true;
    try {
      final newToken = await _refreshToken();
      _tokenStore.setAccessToken(newToken);
      // Retry the original request
      final retryResponse = await _retry(err.requestOptions, newToken);
      handler.resolve(retryResponse);
      // Retry queued requests
      _retryQueuedRequests(newToken);
    } catch (_) {
      _clearAuthAndRedirect();
      handler.next(err);
    } finally {
      _isRefreshing = false;
    }
  } else if (err.response?.statusCode == 401 && _isRefreshing) {
    // Queue this request to retry after refresh completes
    _queueRequest(err.requestOptions, handler);
  } else {
    handler.next(err);
  }
}
```

### 3. Mobile Headers Interceptor
Adds device-specific headers to every request.

```dart
class MobileHeadersInterceptor extends Interceptor {
  @override
  void onRequest(RequestOptions options, RequestInterceptorHandler handler) {
    options.headers.addAll({
      'X-Device-Id': _deviceInfo.deviceId,       // Unique device identifier
      'X-App-Version': _packageInfo.version,      // e.g., "1.2.3"
      'X-Platform': Platform.isIOS ? 'ios' : 'android',
    });
    handler.next(options);
  }
}
```

### 4. Retry Interceptor
- Retries failed requests up to **3 attempts**.
- Retry on: network errors, 408 (timeout), 429 (rate limit), 500+ (server errors).
- Exponential backoff: 1s, 2s, 4s.
- Do NOT retry: 400, 401, 403, 404, 422.

### 5. Logging Interceptor
- Active in **debug mode only** (`kDebugMode`).
- Logs: method, URL, status code, duration.
- NEVER logs: Authorization header value, request/response bodies in production.

### 6. Error Interceptor
Maps Dio errors to typed `AppException` hierarchy.

```dart
class ErrorInterceptor extends Interceptor {
  @override
  void onError(DioException err, ErrorInterceptorHandler handler) {
    final exception = switch (err.type) {
      DioExceptionType.connectionTimeout => const AppException.network('Tempo de conexao esgotado'),
      DioExceptionType.receiveTimeout => const AppException.network('Servidor demorou para responder'),
      DioExceptionType.connectionError => const AppException.network('Sem conexao com a internet'),
      _ => _mapResponseError(err.response),
    };
    handler.next(err.copyWith(error: exception));
  }

  AppException _mapResponseError(Response? response) {
    return switch (response?.statusCode) {
      400 => AppException.badRequest(response?.data['message'] ?? 'Requisicao invalida'),
      401 => const AppException.unauthorized('Sessao expirada'),
      403 => const AppException.forbidden('Sem permissao para esta acao'),
      404 => const AppException.notFound('Recurso nao encontrado'),
      422 => AppException.validation(_parseValidationErrors(response?.data)),
      429 => const AppException.rateLimited('Muitas requisicoes. Aguarde um momento.'),
      _ => AppException.server('Erro no servidor (${response?.statusCode})'),
    };
  }
}
```

## Response Format

### Standard Envelope
The Laravel API returns responses in this format:
```json
{
  "data": { ... },
  "meta": { ... }
}
```

### List / Paginated Response
```json
{
  "data": [ ... ],
  "meta": {
    "current_page": 1,
    "per_page": 15,
    "total": 47,
    "last_page": 4
  }
}
```

### Pagination Model
```dart
@freezed
class PaginatedResponse<T> with _$PaginatedResponse<T> {
  const factory PaginatedResponse({
    required List<T> data,
    required int currentPage,
    required int perPage,
    required int total,
    required int lastPage,
  }) = _PaginatedResponse<T>;
}
```

## Query Parameters

### Sparse Fieldsets
Request only the fields you need to reduce payload size:
```
GET /api/v1/cameras?fields=id,name,status,thumbnail_url
```

### Filtering
```
GET /api/v1/cameras?filter[status]=active&filter[manufacturer]=hikvision
```

### Sorting
```
GET /api/v1/cameras?sort=-created_at   (descending)
GET /api/v1/cameras?sort=name           (ascending)
```

### Pagination
```
GET /api/v1/cameras?page=2&per_page=15
```

### Include Relations
```
GET /api/v1/cameras?include=stream,location
```

## ETag Caching

### Strategy
- Store ETag from response headers.
- Send `If-None-Match` on subsequent requests.
- On 304 Not Modified, return cached data.
- Reduces bandwidth and improves perceived performance.

```dart
class EtagCacheInterceptor extends Interceptor {
  final Map<String, String> _etagStore = {};
  final Map<String, Response> _responseCache = {};

  @override
  void onRequest(RequestOptions options, RequestInterceptorHandler handler) {
    final etag = _etagStore[options.uri.toString()];
    if (etag != null) {
      options.headers['If-None-Match'] = etag;
    }
    handler.next(options);
  }

  @override
  void onResponse(Response response, ResponseInterceptorHandler handler) {
    final etag = response.headers.value('etag');
    if (etag != null) {
      _etagStore[response.requestOptions.uri.toString()] = etag;
      _responseCache[response.requestOptions.uri.toString()] = response;
    }
    handler.next(response);
  }

  @override
  void onError(DioException err, ErrorInterceptorHandler handler) {
    if (err.response?.statusCode == 304) {
      final cached = _responseCache[err.requestOptions.uri.toString()];
      if (cached != null) {
        handler.resolve(cached);
        return;
      }
    }
    handler.next(err);
  }
}
```

## Data Source Pattern

```dart
// lib/data/datasources/remote/camera_remote_data_source.dart
class CameraRemoteDataSource {
  final Dio _dio;

  CameraRemoteDataSource(this._dio);

  Future<PaginatedResponse<CameraDto>> getCameras({
    int page = 1,
    int perPage = 15,
    String? status,
    String? search,
    String? sort,
    List<String>? fields,
  }) async {
    final response = await _dio.get('/cameras', queryParameters: {
      'page': page,
      'per_page': perPage,
      if (status != null) 'filter[status]': status,
      if (search != null) 'filter[search]': search,
      if (sort != null) 'sort': sort,
      if (fields != null) 'fields': fields.join(','),
    });

    return PaginatedResponse.fromJson(
      response.data,
      (json) => CameraDto.fromJson(json as Map<String, dynamic>),
    );
  }
}
```

## Rules

- NEVER hardcode the API base URL — always read from environment.
- NEVER store tokens in SharedPreferences — use `flutter_secure_storage`.
- NEVER log sensitive data (tokens, passwords) even in debug mode.
- NEVER retry 401/403/422 responses — they require user action.
- ALWAYS use the standard response envelope (`data` + `meta`).
- ALWAYS map Dio errors to typed `AppException` for consistent error handling.
- ALWAYS send mobile headers (`X-Device-Id`, `X-App-Version`, `X-Platform`).
- ALWAYS implement token refresh with request queuing to avoid race conditions.
- ALWAYS use sparse fieldsets when the UI only needs a subset of fields.
- ALWAYS handle pagination with the `PaginatedResponse` model.
- ALWAYS use ETag caching for frequently accessed, rarely changing data.
